From d4f44a332e00e7b35105e2003b28f57a58098c14 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mminin <mminin2010@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 15:50:34 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] XFA: Add the data DOM

Forms keep lists of values and their own variables in xfa.datasets, and
immigration forms fill their drop-down lists from there with bindItems.
These lists stayed empty.

The datasets packet now becomes a data DOM of dataGroup and dataValue
nodes named by their tags, reachable from scripts as xfa.datasets,
xfa.data, $data and $record. Scripts can create data nodes, append and
remove them, load and save their XML, read attributes as metadata
values and resolve SOM expressions in them. Saved forms keep the data
DOM.

Also:
- Choice lists take their items from bindItems unless they list their
  own.
- Non-empty values of the initial data go into the fields they match.
- Fields bound with match="global" share their value with all fields of
  the same name.
- xfa.form.remerge() rebuilds the form from the template and its data
  once the running event is over.
- Scripts with runAt="server" do not run, and getDeltas() exists.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
